nely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm irregularly shaped  yellow pink fibromembranous tissue forming the wall of a cystic cavity that was previously opened to reveal an irregular  trabeculated inner lining surface  The wall thickness ranges from REMOVED_DATE   1 0cm  The external surface of the wall is inked black  The internal surface is inked blue for orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable fibroadipose tissue forming the wall of the cyst  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A D  Within the same specimen container are three irregularly shaped  pink yellow soft tissue fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  respectively  Serially sectioning of these soft tissue fragments reveals no gross abnormalities  Representative sections of each fragment are submitted in cassette E  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Andrew H Schulick  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , No.
