assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of firm white breast tissue that on cut sectioning reveals fibrosis  firm adipose tissue and small cysts  entirely submitted in A H  Labeled  1  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm fragment of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm nodular area with microcysts  Entirely submitted in I N  with nodule in K N  Labeled  2  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of breast inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm nodular area  the rest is unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted from 0 W with nodules  area of microcalcification on mammogram  from P S  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  NO INFILTRATING CARCINOMA LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  GROSS DIAGNOSES  2 AND  3  NO GROSS EVIDENCE OF INFILTRATING CARCINOMA O R  Resident  ESTHER OLIVA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  BR