hemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in two parts each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  left modified mastectomy  is a 17 x 10cm ellipse of skin with an eccentrically placed normal appearing nipple overlying a 23 x 15 x 4cm mass of breast tissue with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail at one end  Black suture is present on one edge of the specimen  superior   The epidermal surface shows areas of hyperpigmentation  however  no scar is grossly identified  Sectioning into the specimen shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm cylindrical mass present 2 0cm deep to the epidermis  2 0cm anterior to the deep margin  4 0cm from the inferior margin  6 0cm from the superior margin  15 0cm from the lateral margin  and approximately 7 0cm from the medial margin  On closer inspection  the mass is composed of dense fibrous tissue enveloping areas of more normal appearing fibroadipose tissue causing focal retraction and puckering  1 5cm inferior to this area there is a second 2 0cm in diameter area of gritty  white tissue which is 1 0cm from the closest margin  SECTION CODE A B  Representative sections of deep margin  closer approach in B   C D  Representative sections of tumor mass  E F  Representative random sections of normal breast parenchyma  medial and 