Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 23 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  60   AND CARCINOMA IN SITU CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  40    SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 2cm in greatest diameter and in several sections  extends to two millimeters of the nearest inked resection margin  No vascular invasion is identified  There is a scar with giant cell reaction adjacent to the tumor consistent with previous surgery  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 21 14                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with an needle localizing wire in place and an accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm tan  firm  focally gritty stellate lesion that approaches the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved as frozen  The remaining specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through H  Resident  Robin E  Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT MASS  BIOPSY  CARCINOMA WITH LOBULAR FEATURES  HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Elizabeth Bailey  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , No.
