or orientation as follows  anterior blue  and posterior black  Preliminary gross examination of the specimen in the Frozen Section Lab  does not reveal any grossly suspicious findings  Upon further sectioning  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm white gray  ill defined  slightly firm area  exuding yellow  pasty material is seen  The area is located 1 6cm from the posterior resection margin and 2 1cm from the anterior resection margin  and is within the lower inner quadrant  LIQ  of the mastectomy specimen  The remaining breast parenchyma cut surface consists of dense gray white fibrous tissue with focally gritty areas occupying approximately 60  of the cut surfaces and extending throughout all the 4 quadrants  No other discrete masses are grossly appreciated  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slightly firm  LIQ area  submitted entirely    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin nearest to the slightly firm area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the central area of the specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the upper outer quadrant  UOQ    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the lower outer quadrant  LOQ    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the upper inner quadrant  UIQ   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm right simple mastectomy specimen  bearing a 3 0cm in diameter brown  wrinkled unremarkable areola and an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm everted nipple  There is a tan  wrinkled peripheral rim of skin around the areola measuring 0 5cm in maximum thickness  with a C shaped  well healed scar measuring 3 0cm in length  The specimen is received with a suture designating the 12 o clock aspect  as per the surgeon  and is inked for orientation as follows  anterior   blue  and posterior   black  Sectioning r