he predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 AUG 98 at 09 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a breast biopsy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm with a needle localization wire in place  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned at 0 3cm intervals to reveal a 1 6cm firm white area adjacent to the biopsy tract  This lesion is located at 0 3cm from the superior margin and immediately adjacent to the skin ellipse attached  4 0 x 1 2cm    The specimen is oriented according to the following landmarks  Long stitch superior  short stitch  medial  the deep margin is indicated by a rim of skeletal muscle  Section code  A  Lesion to superior  B  Lesion to skin  C  Additional section of lesion  D  Representative section of unremarkable breast parenchyma to deep margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing numerous lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE up to 2 0cm in largest dimension  Submitted as follows  Section code  continued   E  One lymph node bisected  F I  Additional lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  One of the surfaces is concave and is inked blue  the opposite surface is convex and is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal fibrous breast parenchyma with no focal lesions present  At one of the borders of the specimen there is a small piece of skeletal muscle measuring 1 0cm in largest dimension  The fibrous component of the specimen is entirely submitted in six cassettes as follows  Section code  continued   J O  Starting from the border containing the small piece of skeletal muscle  Resident  ADRIANO PIRIS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1  MARGINS GROSSLY NEGATIVE  O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT   EXISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
