_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm brown skin ellipse  which displays a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm unremarkable nipple areola complex  On the lower lateral aspect of the skin ellipse  there is a 3 0cm healing scar  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior aspect is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 1cm tan red  focally hemorrhagic biopsy cavity  which is located in the lower outer quadrant  The cavity is surrounded by focal areas of tan yellow  indurated fat necrosis  This cavity extends to 1 1cm from the posterior margin  This cavity is contiguous with the healing scar located on the skin surface  The remaining breast tissue is predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue intermixed with a minute amount of tan white fibrous tissue  There are focal areas of blue dye surrounding the biopsy cavity  No other masses or lesions are identified  No lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity to closest deep margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of tissue surrounding biopsy cavity  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right sentinel lymph node  1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan pink glistening lymph node  which is surrounded by a small amount of tan pink to tan yellow adipose tissue  The lymph node is serially sectioned to reveal a tan glistening cut surface  The lymph node is entirely submitted minus the surrounding fat in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right sentinel lymph node  2   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan pink glistening lymph node  which is surrounded by a small amount of tan yellow focally hemorrhagic adipose tissue  The lymph node 